# Git Commit Messages

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) in **English**, aligned with [clowder-ai](https://github.com/zts212653/clowder-ai) style.

## Format

```text
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

[optional body]
```

## Rules

- Subject in English; imperative mood (`add`, not `added` / `Adding`)
- **Subject ≤ 72 characters** (aim ~50); one line only
- Types: `feat` | `fix` | `docs` | `perf` | `refactor` | `test` | `chore` | `ci`
- Scope = package or domain: `core` | `api` | `mcp` | `web` | `harness` | `openspec`
- Body is **optional**. If present: 1–3 short sentences on **why / impact**, not a file checklist
- Do **not** list every touched path, UI detail, or OpenSpec folder in the body — put that in the PR or `openspec/changes/`
- Prefer several small commits over one mega-message when scopes differ
- **Do not over-split.** Aim for a handful of commits per logical change
  (typically 1–3), not one per file/submodule. A single refactor that touches
  `core` + `api` + `web` together is one commit, not three — the scopes are
  part of the same change. Split only when edits are genuinely unrelated.
- Commit in batches by change — group related edits into one commit, separate unrelated edits into their own commits
- Pass the message via HEREDOC; no Chinese in the subject

## Good

```text
feat(core): add verify-loop state machine
fix(mcp): pass bearer auth to tool handlers
docs(adr): record postgres-over-sqlite decision
```

```text
feat(web): add daily workspace sidebar

Learners need plan/queue and notes in one place for same-day review.
```

## Bad

```text
feat(core): add daily plan, notes, chat persistence and web workspace

- gotit.db: SQLAlchemy async models ...
- api.routes: /v1/days ...
- web: Apple-style ...
```

(Too long; reads like a changelog. Split commits or move detail to the PR.)

```text
refactor(core): split db.ops into day module
refactor(core): split db.ops into note module
refactor(core): split db.ops into claim module
refactor(api): split routes health endpoint
refactor(api): split routes ingest endpoint
...
```

(Over-split. One cohesive `db.ops` refactor should be a single commit, not
one per submodule. Group related edits; split only unrelated work.)
